            return False
```

It catches `ValueError`.

If `self.__file.isatty()` raises `ValueError`, my `isatty` method will propagate it, and `rich/console.py` will catch it and return `False`. This is correct.

So the only thing I need to handle is `AttributeError` to avoid breaking the case where `self.__file` doesn't have `isatty`.

